## Units

| # | Unit and compelling question | Days | Skills | Owned standards | Practices | What students learn | Why this unit, here | Check set adds | Sensitive topics and teacher notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Where my plan stands. What do I know now about myself and the world of work, and which three clusters will I study? Hook: one invented worker's plan at 14, at 16 and at 25, and what changed it. | 12 | g10-cd3-r4-grouping-that-helps; g10-cd2-values-in-choice; g10-all2-learner-moments; g10-all1-r3-study-habits-review; g10-all1-r5-school-plan-review; g10-cd2-r2-compare-models; g10-cd1-a3-goal-steps | CD3.R4; CD2.A5; CD2.R5; ALL2.A2; ALL2.R2; ALL1.R3; ALL1.R5; CD2.R2; CD1.A3 | None placed (practice 10 retrieved from grade 8 on the plan; unit 4 places it) | In this order: the plan reopened from grade 8, or begun, on the full plan template, the models introduced again for every student (plan, job card, cluster map, decision steps card, data table, portfolio), and dated near and far goals with steps already taken (CD1.A3), two days; values in a choice, named privately and weighed (CD2.A5, CD2.R5), and two learning moments traced privately (ALL2.A2, ALL2.R2); a week's study log begun, rated on the plan day with one habit chosen to strengthen (ALL1.R3), and what the grade 8 school plan achieved, with the high school course plan revised (ALL1.R5; a student new to the course reviews last year's courses instead); the same twenty jobs sorted by cluster, by training level and by work setting, and which grouping helps the plan most (CD3.R4), two days; field task over two days: the class argues for its two shared clusters with the decision steps and a weighted criteria table, tallies the ballot on the data table, and each student chooses their own cluster with both methods and says which suits them (CD2.R2). Carried from grade 8 at higher demand (owned there, retaught for a student new to the course): CD3.K4; CD3.A4; CD2.K5; ALL2.K2; ALL1.K3; ALL1.A3; ALL1.K5; ALL1.A5; CD2.K2; CD2.A2; CD1.K3; CD1.R3. The first plan line of school results is drafted here and checked in unit 4 (g10-all1-school-results). Out: a scored interest instrument (none is adapted); the job pick (unit 4) | It opens the course because every later unit needs the plan, the models and the three clusters, and the lens's order starts with the self before the world of work. It introduces again every model for a student who did not take Career Exploration (an optional course, lesson 32). Readiness items in day 1's last ten minutes: a percent of a total and a dated pay figure (APPROACH unit field 4), the plan's parts and the decision steps (g8-cd1-2-first-plan, g8-cd2-2-decision-steps, last used in Exploration unit 1, grade 8). | Candidate: one unseen item reading a dated pay figure on a new job card; the decision steps and a weighted table run on an invented student's choice of cluster. | No task asks about family income or work. Values and learning moments are private on the plan page; the plan is scored on its reasoning, never on the cluster chosen. The ballot is the class's, and a student's own cluster is theirs; no student is steered. Tools: a private plan template (paper path) and a dated job profile on one shared screen; Curio Class writes the full plan template, the twenty sort cards, the weighted criteria table, the ballot tally sheet, the cluster map at program-of-study depth and the invented worker's three plans. Cost, class of 30, provisional (ours, 2026-11-25): printing about 300 pages, about $15 at $0.05 a page; no supplies. Sensitivity read: disabled workers among the sort cards, and first-generation students (the agent checks no task assumes a parent who knows the high school or college system; it first studies the federal Office of Disability Employment Policy's pages, https://www.dol.gov/agencies/odep, and disability-led organizations' published pages on work). |
