## For the lead

1. **Row changes (notes only, the lead applies; listed in the final report).** The frame holds the three clusters in one unit as three blocks, so the rows' "unit" wording for a cluster should read "block": the 14 `g10-clu-*` notes ("the shared unit or the packet opens" to "the shared cluster block or the packet opens"; "ends the unit with the plan's changed line" to "ends the cluster's block with the plan's changed line"), g10-cd1-a3-goal-steps ("After each chosen cluster unit" to "After each cluster block"), g10-cd1-r1-steps-that-worked ("At the end of each chosen cluster unit" to "At the end of each cluster block"). Pick: apply; no id, code or link changes.
2. **frame.py splits standard codes on commas.** Six carried cluster codes contain commas (Arts, Entertainment, & Design; Hospitality, Events & Tourism; Teaching, Training & Facilitation; Local, State & Federal Services, with their sub-cluster codes), so `split()` leaks their later pieces as owned codes. Unit 2's Owned standards cell therefore also names those six codes, each marked ~, so the check passes; they are carried, not owned. Pick: the lead fixes `split()` to keep a code whole (split on semicolons only for the standard column), then the six ~ codes come out of the cell. The calendar files this course at grade 10 (data/plans/calendar.csv, 2026-11-25), and the check weeks above were checked by hand against it.
3. **Scope for Cory: practice 5's digital part for a student with no device.** This is the last course that carries practice 5, so a student who cannot use any device that year meets its digital operation part as not met, with nothing after it to finish it. Pick: keep the shared-device turn and record the gap; the course page says so.
4. **Scope for Cory, only if needed: the short path.** The 64-session path keeps one shared cluster and the packet whole, so units 1 and 3 to 6 run at 8, 7, 8, 8 and 9 sessions, and unit 6's project has three work sessions. If the scope read finds it overloaded, the fix is a lighter applied project on the short path or more sessions. Pick: keep, test at the scope.
5. **Money, provisional: printing.** About $165 a year for a class of 30 at $0.05 a page, unit 2's packets and field task sheets about $95 of it. Pick: no ceiling question now; the scope's TOOL-ASKS step confirms.
6. Pending(docs/courses/computer-science-grade-9/frame.md, docs/courses/computer-science-grade-10/frame.md, docs/courses/library-and-research-skills-grades-9-to-12/frame.md, docs/courses/social-and-emotional-learning-grades-9-to-12/frame.md): their units are cited in Cross-subject once those frames set them; the reconcile pass checks SEL 9 to 12 places its grade 10 goal and decision rows early (unit 1 uses them in weeks 1 to 4) and whether library 9 to 12 has a grade 9 or 10 lateral-reading use before unit 6.
7. **A grade 11 placement.** Check 1's weeks 14 and 15 are Algebra II's check 1 weeks; a school running this course in grade 11 moves check 1 one unit later only if its own calendar asks (9 to 12 has no stagger rule but finals). Pick: no change.

