Handed on to later grades: none. Career Pathways is the last career education course (data/progressions/cte-edges.md), and no row here has a `hands_on`. Where the threads end: the full plan to a first credential (unit 4) and the portfolio presented to a panel (unit 6) go home with the student at the end of the year; after this course the plan's next owner is the school's counselor and its state's required plan, where a school has one (STANDARD.md section 4). One's own money, a later thread, is grade 12 Economics' (STANDARD.md section 5), not a lean.

