## Course-level checks

Both checks avoid the grade 10 core check weeks (docs/courses/CALENDAR.md: ELA 9, 18, 32; geometry 10, 21, 32; chemistry 11, 20 to 21, 32; world history II 8 to 9, 18 to 19, 32), as the after-core rule asks; grades 9 to 12 have no rule but the finals week (stagger rule 4), and the year-end check uses week 32, the finals week. Check 1 falls on course days 42 and 43 (school days 70 and 72, weeks 14 and 15): no grade 10 core subject has a check day there, and for a grade 9 placement weeks 14 and 15 are also clear (ELA grade 9's respond day is school day 66; Algebra I's checks are weeks 12 to 13 and 22; biology's week 16). Check 2 falls on course days 95 and 96 (school days 159 and 160), beside every core subject's year-end check.

