|---|---|---|---|---|
| Course-level check 1, mid-year | 2 (days 42 and 43) | 1 | 1 | Samples units 1 and 2's two shared blocks, since unit 2's packet was assessed two course days earlier, with its respond day between: a new, unseen job card with new figures from a cluster outside the student's three (four cards are prepared, from Travel and Leisure, Marine Transportation, Insurance and Ecological Research and Development, four different clusters, so at least one lies outside any student's three), read for training route, pay and outlook with source and year (unit 2); two data items, a rate and a percent from a dated table (units 1 and 2); the decision steps and the weighted table run on an invented student's choice between two programs of study, defended with one figure (unit 1). Unit 2's scored pieces are reused unscored only as the teacher's record. Respond day: groups from the missed items, at most four, and the plan line the check changed |
| Course-level check 2, year-end | 6 (days 95 and 96) | 1 | 1 | Samples units 3 to 5, since unit 6 was assessed two course days earlier, with its respond day between: an unseen percent change from two dated projections and an unseen regional pay item (unit 3); an invented posting in two versions with the same questions and criteria (a field outside the student's chosen job's cluster), read against a resume line, and the line revised for that reader (unit 5); one full plan line defended with a dated figure and one trade-off named, scored on its reasoning (unit 4). Unit 6's panel record is reused unscored as the record. Respond day: the plan revised from the check, and the plan and portfolio sent home |

