g10-prac-8-creativity | ~CTE.Career Ready Practices.8
Carries practice 8 (~; first taught in a task in grade 8) on Pathways field tasks at higher demand. In a field task and the applied project the student generates several ideas, combines two into a new one, and tests it against the field's real constraint (cost, a code rule, a time limit); look-fors: more than one idea, a combination, tested against the constraint. The practice is judged with those look-fors on the piece, never on a list. Assumes g8-prac-8-creativity. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-prac-9-resources | ~CTE.Career Ready Practices.9
Carries practice 9 (~; first taught in a task in grade 8) on Pathways field tasks at higher demand. On the field tasks the student keeps an employer's materials and labor hours within an invented budget, and compares a dated entry wage with the time and cost of training to the first credential; look-fors: stays in budget, arithmetic shown, waste noted. Limit: never a student's or family's own money (one's own money is taught in grade 12 Economics, social-studies econ-earning-income and econ-spending-consumer; not a lean, since it comes later). The practice is judged with those look-fors on the piece, never on a list. Assumes g8-prac-9-resources. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-prac-10-plan-path | ~CTE.Career Ready Practices.10
Carries practice 10 (~; first taught in a task in grade 8) on Pathways field tasks at higher demand. The student builds the full plan (its home row is g10-all2-full-plan; this row judges practice 10 on it) to the first credential of the student's chosen job, the narrow end of the broad-to-narrow path (high school courses, a training route, the credential, time and cost, a fallback) and revises it from written feedback; look-fors: every step linked to a strength or interest, a dated figure behind each route, a revision made. No route is the default. The practice is judged with those look-fors on the piece, never on a list. Assumes g8-prac-10-plan-path. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-prac-11-effects | ~CTE.Career Ready Practices.11
Carries practice 11 (~; first taught in a task in grade 8) on Pathways field tasks at higher demand. The student maps the people, place and environment the applied project's decision affects, near and far, and changes the decision once for a better effect; look-fors: people and place both named, one effect weighed with a figure, the decision changed or kept with a reason. The practice is judged with those look-fors on the piece, never on a list. Assumes g8-prac-11-effects. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-prac-12-academic-skills | ~CTE.Career Ready Practices.12
Carries practice 12 (~; first taught in a task in grade 8) on Pathways field tasks at higher demand. The course's applied project: the student takes a real problem from the field of their chosen job (STANDARD.md section 3, "Broad to narrow"), solves it with the field's math, reading and science, and defends the choice with data to a small panel; the best piece goes in the portfolio with a sentence on why; look-fors: the school skill named where used, the choice backed by a figure with its source, a limit stated. The practice is judged with those look-fors on the piece, never on a list. Assumes g8-prac-12-academic-skills. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd1-r1-steps-that-worked | CD1.R1; ~CD1.K1; ~CD1.A1
Owns CD1.R1: the student judges which planning steps since grade 8 actually moved them forward, with one piece of evidence for each, checked on the plan page. Carries CD1.K1 and CD1.A1 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. At the end of each chosen cluster unit the student marks which plan steps moved them forward and explains why the plan stays open after the first credential. Assumes g8-cd1-1-plan-keeps-going. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd1-r2-revise-plan | CD1.R2; ~CD1.K2; ~CD1.A2
Owns CD1.R2: after written feedback on the full plan, the student marks the lines that no longer fit and revises them, each with a reason; scored on the reasoning, never on the path chosen. Carries CD1.K2 and CD1.A2 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The grade 8 plan is reopened in the first unit and rebuilt on the full plan template (program of study, credential, time and cost); the career-plan model returns from grade 8 after the year with no career education course. Assumes g8-cd1-2-first-plan. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd1-a3-goal-steps | CD1.A3; ~CD1.K3; ~CD1.R3
Owns CD1.A3: the student shows steps already taken toward a near goal (a course chosen, a question asked of a counselor) and a far goal, checked against the dated goals on the plan. Carries CD1.K3 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student sets dated near and far goals for the full plan, each tied to a step in the program of study. Carries CD1.R3 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. After each chosen cluster unit the student revisits the goals and changes one that shifted, with the reason on the plan's change log. Assumes g8-cd1-3-goals and g8-cd1-3r-revisit-goals. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd1-steering-habits | CD1.A4; CD1.R4; ~CD1.K4
CD1.A4: in a field task that fails on the first try the student shows where they adapted or bounced back, checked in the task reflection. CD1.R4: the student rates their own steering habits from that evidence and picks one to grow, checked on the plan page. Carries CD1.K4 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student names the steering habits in a worker's account of a career change in a chosen field. Assumes g8-cd1-4-steering-habits. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd1-r5-plan-keeps-up | CD1.R5; ~CD1.K5; ~CD1.A5
Owns CD1.R5: the student judges how well the full plan keeps up with changes in themselves and in work, using one dated outlook figure, checked on the plan's change log. Carries CD1.K5 and CD1.A5 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student records each change since grade 8 on the plan's change log with its cause (a new interest, a dated outlook figure). Assumes g8-cd1-5-plans-change. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd2-r1-decide-review | CD2.R1; ~CD2.K1; ~CD2.A1
Owns CD2.R1: after choosing their own cluster and their job the student weighs what worked and what did not in the way they decided, checked in a short written reflection. Carries CD2.K1 and CD2.A1 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. Before choosing their own cluster the student describes their own way of deciding and recalls a school choice that shows it. Assumes g8-cd2-1-how-i-decide. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd2-r2-compare-models | CD2.R2; ~CD2.K2; ~CD2.A2
Owns CD2.R2: the student makes the same choice with the decision steps and with a weighted table, compares the two, and says which suits them and why, checked on both worked tables. Carries CD2.K2 and CD2.A2 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The decision-steps model returns from grade 8: the student uses it to choose their own cluster, and to argue for the class's two shared clusters, with a weighted criteria table. Assumes g8-cd2-2-decision-steps. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd2-r3-enough-facts | CD2.R3; ~CD2.K3; ~CD2.A3
Owns CD2.R3: before the applied project's defense (g10-prac-12-academic-skills) the student judges whether enough good facts stand behind the decision and adds what is missing, checked on the evidence list. Carries CD2.K3 and CD2.A3 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student uses facts about self, jobs and schooling to pick the first credential in the full plan. Assumes g8-cd2-3-facts-for-choices. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd2-r4-search-wide | CD2.R4; ~CD2.K4; ~CD2.A4
Owns CD2.R4: the student judges how widely they searched before choosing the first credential (routes, programs, places counted) and widens it once, checked on the options list. Carries CD2.K4 and CD2.A4 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student lists at least three routes to the same job in a chosen field with their likely results. Assumes g8-cd2-4-options. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd2-values-in-choice | CD2.A5; CD2.R5; ~CD2.K5
CD2.A5: the student points out where their values show in the cluster choice, checked on the private plan page. CD2.R5: the student weighs how much those values steered the choice and whether they want that, checked in a short reflection. Carries CD2.K5 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student names the values behind their cluster choice on the plan page, kept private. Assumes g8-cd2-5-values. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd2-experience-shapes | CD2.A6; CD2.R6; ~CD2.K6
CD2.A6: the student shows how a school or work experience (a class, a club, a job, a field task) shaped a choice, theirs or an invented worker's, checked on a short piece. CD2.R6: the student judges how much experiences have shaped their choices so far, checked in a reflection. Teacher note: answered from school or work, or for an invented worker, never from family circumstances (STANDARD.md sections 3 and 6). Carries CD2.K6 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student explains, for invented workers in the chosen fields, how school, work and home life shaped a decision. Never asked of a student's own family circumstances (STANDARD.md section 6). Assumes g8-cd2-6-life-shapes-choices. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd2-stereotype-check | CD2.A7; CD2.R7; ~CD2.K7
CD2.A7: the student finds a time a stereotype narrowed a choice, their own or a worker's from a public profile, checked on a short piece. CD2.R7: the student writes a plan to catch and set aside stereotypes when choosing, checked against the plan's next choice. Carries CD2.K7 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student finds stereotypes in invented job ads and images for a chosen field and rewrites one. Assumes g8-cd2-7-stereotypes. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd2-luck-and-control | CD2.A8; CD2.R8; ~CD2.K8
CD2.A8: the student tells of a time luck played a part in a choice, their own or a worker's from a public profile, checked on a short piece. CD2.R8: the student judges how much luck shaped earlier choices and names what they can still control, checked in a reflection. Carries CD2.K8 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student reads public worker profiles in a chosen field for a lucky break and its timing. Assumes g8-cd2-8-luck-timing. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd2-r9-trade-offs | CD2.R9; ~CD2.K9; ~CD2.A9
Owns CD2.R9: the student judges how well they handle the trade-offs in the full plan (time, cost, place, pay), checked on the plan's trade-off line. Carries CD2.K9 and CD2.A9 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student names the trade-offs between two jobs in their three clusters, from their job cards. Assumes g8-cd2-9-trade-offs. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd3-r1-check-plan-info | CD3.R1; ~CD3.K1; ~CD3.A1
Owns CD3.R1: the student checks the full plan against current, fair information from the dated data sheets and updates each out-of-date line, checked on the plan. Carries CD3.K1 and CD3.A1 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. Each cluster data sheet changes at least one plan line, and the student says which figure did it. Assumes g8-cd3-1-why-career-info. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd3-r2-combine-facts | CD3.R2; ~CD3.K2; ~CD3.A2
Owns CD3.R2: the student judges how well the full plan combines job, training, hiring and economic facts, with a matrix of which fact supports which line, checked on the matrix. Carries CD3.K2 and CD3.A2 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The job study grows: four kinds of information (job, training, hiring, economy), local and national, for a job in each chosen cluster; the job-card model returns from grade 8. Assumes g8-cd3-2-job-study. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd3-r3-rate-sources | CD3.R3; ~CD3.K3; ~CD3.A3
Owns CD3.R3: the student rates each source in the applied project and the full plan for accuracy, fairness, date and completeness on a source log, checked on the log. Carries CD3.K3 and CD3.A3 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The lateral-reading model returns from grade 8 on harder career sources: a training school's ad, a job board post and a machine-made career summary. Assumes g8-cd3-3-judge-sources. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd3-r4-grouping-that-helps | CD3.R4; ~CD3.K4; ~CD3.A4
Owns CD3.R4: the student sorts the same jobs by cluster, by training level and by work setting, and judges which grouping helps their plan most, checked on the three sorts. Carries CD3.K4 and CD3.A4 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The cluster-map model returns from grade 8: the student uses it to choose their own cluster, to find sub-clusters within their three clusters and to narrow to one sub-cluster and one named job (STANDARD.md section 3, "Broad to narrow"). Assumes g8-cd3-4-cluster-map. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd3-r5-open-to-jobs | CD3.R5; ~CD3.K5; ~CD3.A5
Owns CD3.R5: the student judges how open they have been to jobs outside the usual pattern for their group, counting the job cards they made, checked in a private reflection; the group may stay unnamed, and the teacher checks the reflection for a reason, never for which group. Carries CD3.K5 and CD3.A5 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student studies seriously one job in a chosen cluster that few people of a group the student chooses hold (it may be their own, kept private; the student never states their group in class). Assumes g8-cd3-5-open-jobs. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd3-a6-uncommon-in-plan | CD3.A6; ~CD3.K6
Owns CD3.A6: the student decides for themselves whether a job uncommon for their group belongs in their plan and writes why, checked for a reason, never for the answer; the plan stays private. Teacher note: pay and job gaps by sex and race are shown with a dated source, never as a verdict on a person; first-generation, rural and tribal students and students who already care for family or work are planned for; every section of the pay-gap unit carries health's "if a student tells you something" steps on its teacher page. Carries CD3.K6 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student lists gains and hurdles of a job uncommon for a group in a chosen field from dated figures and real workers' accounts. Assumes g8-cd3-6-uncommon-jobs. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd4-work-skills | CD4.A1; CD4.R1; ~CD4.K1
CD4.A1: in a job simulation (a first week in an invented workplace from a chosen field, with a supervisor feedback card) the student uses their skills to get, keep and grow in the job, checked against the card's look-fors. CD4.R1: the student rates their work skills from that feedback and plans how to build the weakest, checked on the plan page. Carries CD4.K1 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student sorts the skills in a chosen job's program of study into school, job-specific and general skills. Assumes g8-cd4-1-skill-kinds. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd4-resume-interview | CD4.A2; CD4.R2; ~CD4.K2
CD4.A2: the student writes a resume (a school address or none), a cover letter for an invented posting in a chosen field, fills in an invented application, and does a mock interview with the teacher or a card as the interviewer after a model answer. CD4.R2: the student judges each piece against the criteria before the written feedback and revision, checked on the rubric. Teacher note: no question an employer may not lawfully ask and nothing private (no family income, immigration or work status, record or health), as STANDARD.md section 6 sets. The teacher page states plainly that an employer may not ask about a disability before a job offer, that a worker may ask for a reasonable change to how the job is done, and that a student never has to disclose a disability in a course task. Carries CD4.K2 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The steps of a job search frame the resume and mock interview unit. Assumes g8-cd4-2-job-search-steps. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd4-r3-general-skills-evidence | CD4.R3; ~CD4.K3; ~CD4.A3
Owns CD4.R3: the student rates their general work skills with evidence from the field tasks logged in the portfolio, checked for an example behind each rating. Carries CD4.K3 and CD4.A3 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student shows general work skills in each field task and logs the evidence for the portfolio. Assumes g8-cd4-3-general-skills. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd4-carry-over | CD4.A4; CD4.R4; ~CD4.K4
CD4.A4: the student shows which of their skills would carry to a job in another chosen cluster, checked on two job cards. CD4.R4: the student judges how those carry-over skills widen their options, checked on the plan's fallback line. Carries CD4.K4 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student explains how skills carry between jobs in their three clusters. Assumes g8-cd4-4-carry-over-skills. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd4-moving | CD4.A5; CD4.R5; ~CD4.K5
CD4.A5: from the data sheets' figures by region the student decides where they would be willing to live and work and why, checked for a figure behind the reason. CD4.R5: the student weighs how that choice fits their career goals, checked in the plan. Teacher note: staying close to home is a real choice (family care, tribal and rural ties); no student is asked about family circumstances. Carries CD4.K5 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The data sheets show pay and outlook by region; the student explains how moving or staying changes the options. Assumes g8-cd4-5-moving-for-work. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd4-self-employment-decision | CD4.A6; CD4.R6; ~CD4.K6
CD4.A6: the student decides whether working for themselves belongs in their plan, with the figures from a chosen field, checked for a reason. CD4.R6: the student weighs how that decision fits their goals, checked on the plan. Carries CD4.K6 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student lists the upsides and risks of self-employment in a chosen field from dated figures. Assumes g8-cd4-6-self-employment. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd4-portfolio | CD4.K7; CD4.A7
CD4.K7: the student names ways to present themselves well to an employer (a portfolio, a resume, an interview, a follow-up note), checked on a short list with an example of each. CD4.A7: the student presents the portfolio to a small panel as to an employer and answers questions about it, checked on the rubric. The portfolio model, introduced in grade 8, returns after the year with no career education course. Assumes g8-prac-12-academic-skills (which introduces the portfolio). Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd5-a1-society-needs-plan | CD5.A1; ~CD5.K1
Owns CD5.A1: the student shows how the full plan could adjust if a society need behind the chosen field changed, checked on the plan's fallback line. Carries CD5.K1 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student names a society need behind demand in a chosen field (an aging population, a housing need). Assumes g8-cd5-1-society-needs. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd5-a2-economy-plan | CD5.A2; ~CD5.K2
Owns CD5.A2: from a dated table of the chosen field through a recent downturn, the student shows how the plan could adjust as the economy changes, checked for a figure behind the change. Carries CD5.K2 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student reads a dated table of one chosen field's jobs through a recent economic change. Assumes g8-cd5-2-economic-conditions. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-cd5-a3-hiring-trends-plan | CD5.A3; ~CD5.K3
Owns CD5.A3: from dated outlook projections the student computes the percent change for two jobs and shows how the plan could adjust, checked for the figure and its year. Carries CD5.K3 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student reads dated outlook projections for the chosen fields in a table. Assumes g8-cd5-3-hiring-trends. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all1-school-results | ALL1.A1; ALL1.R1; ~ALL1.K1
ALL1.A1: the student sets out in the full plan the school results the first credential needs (courses, a level in math or reading) and the steps to reach them, checked on the plan. ALL1.R1: midyear the student checks their progress toward those results, checked privately with the teacher; no grade is shared with the class. Carries ALL1.K1 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student links each school result the full plan needs to a goal. Assumes g8-all1-1-school-and-goals. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all1-r2-improve-review | ALL1.R2; ~ALL1.K2; ~ALL1.A2
Owns ALL1.R2: the student reviews how they improved a field task piece from feedback and plans the next step, checked on the revision note. Carries ALL1.K2 and ALL1.A2 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student uses a way of improving school work on a field task piece revised from feedback. Assumes g8-all1-2-improve-schoolwork. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all1-r3-study-habits-review | ALL1.R3; ~ALL1.K3; ~ALL1.A3
Owns ALL1.R3: the student rates their study habits against a week's log and plans to strengthen one, checked on the log. Carries ALL1.K3 and ALL1.A3 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student uses a study habit to prepare a program of study course and notes what it changed. Assumes g8-all1-3-study-habits. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all1-r4-strategies-review | ALL1.R4; ~ALL1.K4; ~ALL1.A4
Owns ALL1.R4: the student judges which learning strategies worked on a field task and changes one that did not, checked in a reflection with the result. No fixed learning-style label is used. Carries ALL1.K4 and ALL1.A4 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student uses what helps them learn to prepare a field task. No fixed learning-style label is used; the row teaches strategies and conditions. Assumes g8-all1-4-what-helps-me-learn. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all1-r5-school-plan-review | ALL1.R5; ~ALL1.K5; ~ALL1.A5
Owns ALL1.R5: the student checks what the grade 8 school plan achieved and revises the high school course plan, checked on the plan. Carries ALL1.K5 and ALL1.A5 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student writes the high school course plan inside the full plan. Assumes g8-all1-5-school-plan. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all1-r6-habits-review | ALL1.R6; ~ALL1.K6; ~ALL1.A6
Owns ALL1.R6: the student judges which attitudes and habits helped or held them back in the applied project, with one example each, checked in a reflection. Carries ALL1.K6 and ALL1.A6 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student shows attitudes and habits that help in the applied project. Assumes g8-all1-6-attitude-habits. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all1-school-widens | ALL1.A7; ALL1.R7; ~ALL1.K7
ALL1.A7: the student shows how their school work widens job options in their three clusters, checked on two job cards. ALL1.R7: the student judges how well their school skills will carry into work, checked against a chosen job's skill list. Carries ALL1.K7 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student shows how a course taken now opens options in a chosen field. Assumes g8-all1-7-school-opens-options. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all1-information-use | ALL1.A8; ALL1.R8; ~ALL1.K8
ALL1.A8: the student shows how finding and using information helped the applied project, checked on the source log. ALL1.R8: the student rates how well they find and use information and plans one improvement, checked in a reflection. Carries ALL1.K8 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student finds and uses information for the applied project with a source log. Assumes g8-all1-8-finding-information. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all2-changing-work | ALL2.A1; ALL2.R1; ~ALL2.K1
ALL2.A1: the student shows how something they learn now prepares them for a dated change in a chosen field, checked on a short piece. ALL2.R1: the student judges whether their skills are ready for a changing, mixed workplace, checked in a reflection. Carries ALL2.K1 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student explains why a chosen field's workers keep learning, from a dated change in the field. Assumes g8-all2-1-lifelong-learning. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all2-learner-moments | ALL2.A2; ALL2.R2; ~ALL2.K2
ALL2.A2: the student gives an example of how learning is part of who they are, checked on a short piece. ALL2.R2: the student traces two learning moments that changed how they see themselves, checked in a reflection, kept private. Carries ALL2.K2 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student explains how seeing themselves as a learner shapes their plan. Assumes g8-all2-2-learner-identity. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all2-r3-learn-on-own | ALL2.R3; ~ALL2.K3; ~ALL2.A3
Owns ALL2.R3: the student judges how well they learned on their own in the applied project, with evidence, checked in a reflection. Carries ALL2.K3 and ALL2.A3 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student carries out a piece of learning alone for the applied project. Assumes g8-all2-3-own-learning. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all2-r4-ready-after-high-school | ALL2.R4; ~ALL2.K4; ~ALL2.A4
Owns ALL2.R4: the student judges how ready they are for the step after high school against a checklist for their route, checked on the plan. Carries ALL2.K4 and ALL2.A4 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The grade 8 move into high school becomes the next move: the student names what the step after high school takes and prepares for it in the full plan. Assumes g8-all2-4-move-to-high-school. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all2-route-steps | ALL2.A5; ALL2.R5; ~ALL2.K5
ALL2.A5: the student shows the steps they are taking toward one route after school (a course, a visit a school arranges, a question to a counselor), checked on the plan. ALL2.R5: the student weighs how that route fits their goals against one other route, checked for figures on time and cost. No route is the default. Teacher note: the military is one real route with its costs and returns, neither promoted nor condemned; no recruiter material appears on a student page, and the school's own policy governs recruiter visits. Carries ALL2.K5 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student names the routes after school (college, trade school, apprenticeship, the military, online study, training on the job) for a job in each chosen cluster. Assumes g8-all2-5-routes-after-school. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all2-full-plan | ALL2.A6; ALL2.R6; ~ALL2.K6
The full plan to a first credential, where the broad-to-narrow path ends (STANDARD.md section 3, "Broad to narrow"): from one of their three clusters the student picks a sub-cluster, then one named job in it, the job they choose, and studies it in depth (its tasks, its training route, its pay and outlook figures, each with its source and year), with one plan step toward it, and the full plan narrows to that job. ALL2.A6: the student chooses a program of study for that job and shows how it fits their plan (high school courses, the training route, the credential, time and cost, a fallback), checked on the plan. ALL2.R6: the student judges how that program prepares them for a changing economy, with a dated outlook figure, checked on the plan's change line. Scored on reasoning, never on the path chosen. Carries ALL2.K6 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student names the programs (a pathway, a major, an apprenticeship) for a job in a chosen cluster. Assumes g8-all2-6-programs. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.
g10-all2-in-and-out-of-class | ALL2.A7; ALL2.R7; ~ALL2.K7
ALL2.A7: the student shows learning they do outside class (a club, a job, a project, any work-based learning the school adds), checked on a portfolio entry; a student with none uses a class project. ALL2.R7: the student judges how their learning in and out of class fit together, checked in a reflection. Carries ALL2.K7 (~; owned in grade 8) at higher demand. The student describes learning outside class that builds skills for a chosen field. Assumes g8-all2-7-learning-outside-class. Grade 9 is skipped because no career education course owns there.

