g10-sub-agriculture-water-systems | Field task day. From an invented district's dated rainfall and water use table, the student splits a limited supply among farms by a given rule, writes the notice to users, and defends the split with the figures. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as an irrigation technician (on-the-job training), a water treatment operator (certificate and a state license) and a hydrologist (four-year study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-arts-design-design-digital | Field task day at higher demand than grade 8. The student answers an invented client brief through two rounds of client feedback, keeps a short style guide, checks text against a given color contrast rule, and quotes the job at a given hourly rate, defended against the brief. The student also maps the program of study for one job, such as a production artist (certificate or self-taught route), a graphic designer (two-year or four-year study) and an art director (experience): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-arts-design-fashion-interiors | Field task day. On graph paper the student lays out a room for an invented client to a budget and a given wheelchair clearance rule, and defends the layout with the cost and the measurements. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as an upholsterer or sewer (on-the-job training), an interior designer (two-year or four-year study; some states license) and a fashion designer (two-year or four-year study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-arts-design-fine-arts | Field task day. The student plans a small show of their own or invented work: a short artist's statement, a price list from an invented materials and hours table, and a hanging plan, defending one price with the figures. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a gallery assistant (on-the-job training), a working artist (any route) and an art teacher (four-year study and a license): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-arts-design-lighting-sound | Field task day. The student writes a cue sheet and stage plot for an invented school assembly and checks the power load from a given watts table against a circuit limit, defending the plan with the load figure. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a stagehand (on-the-job training), an audio and video technician (certificate or two-year study) and a lighting designer (four-year study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-arts-design-media-production | Field task day. The student storyboards a sixty-second school news piece with a shot list and a time budget per shot, lists the consent each person on camera gives, and defends the cut with the timings. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a production assistant (on-the-job training), a camera operator or editor (two-year study) and a producer (four-year study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-arts-design-performing-arts | Field task day. The student builds a rehearsal schedule for an invented community play from a cast availability table and reads dated hourly pay and hours for performers, defending the schedule and naming what the figures say about steady income. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a performer (training through study or practice), a stage manager (two-year or four-year study) and a drama teacher (four-year study and a license): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-construction-skilled-trades | Field task day at higher demand than grade 8. The student makes a full material and labor estimate for a small room job from a floor plan, checks one item against a given code rule, and writes the bid, defended with the arithmetic; the apprenticeship route (hours, pay while training, and a license at the end where the trade and the state require one) is mapped. The student also maps the program of study for one job, such as an apprentice electrician or carpenter (apprenticeship), a licensed electrician or plumber (apprenticeship and, in most states, a license) and a contractor (license rules vary by state): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-construction-architecture-civil | Field task day. From an invented site plan, the student redesigns an entrance ramp to a given slope rule (one unit of rise to twelve of run), finds its length and landings, and defends the design with the figures. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a civil engineering technician (two-year study), a drafter (certificate or two-year study) and a civil engineer or architect (four-year or professional study and a license): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-construction-construction-planning | Field task day. The student estimates and schedules an invented shed build: a material takeoff from a price sheet, crew days and a weather delay, and defends the bid with a contingency percent. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a construction laborer (on-the-job training), a cost estimator (four-year study, or years in a trade) and a construction manager (four-year study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-construction-equipment | Field task day. The student picks which machine to rent for an invented site job from a table of capacity, day rate and operator certification, completes a pre-use inspection checklist from a picture, and defends the choice with the figures. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as an equipment operator (apprenticeship), a heavy equipment mechanic (two-year study) and a site superintendent (experience): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-education-teaching | Field task day at higher demand than grade 8. The student plans and teaches a fifteen-minute lesson to a small group with a check before and after, compares the two results, and revises the lesson from the figures. The student also maps the program of study for one job, such as a teacher aide (high school, and in many schools two years of college or a state test), a corporate trainer (four-year study or experience) and a classroom teacher (four-year study and a state license): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-education-early-childhood | Field task day. The student plans a play-based activity for invented four-year-olds with a given adult-to-child ratio and a safety check, and defends the staffing with the ratio. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a child care worker (certificate or a child development credential), a preschool teacher (two-year or four-year study) and a center director (experience and study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-education-ed-leadership | Field task day. From an invented school's dated attendance table by grade, the student proposes one change, writes a short note to families, and defends the change with the figures. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a school office manager (on-the-job training), an instructional coach (four-year study and experience) and a principal (graduate study and a license): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-education-learner-support | Field task day. From an invented learner's short skills check, the student plans a tutoring session with one goal and a check at the end, and plans the reminder for a family night from last year's invented turnout figures. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a paraprofessional (high school, and in many schools two years of college or a state test), a community engagement coordinator (four-year study) and a school counselor (graduate study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-energy-resources-utilities | Field task day at higher demand than grade 8. From an invented town district's year of use by month and one day's use by hour, the student finds the peak month and the peak hours, proposes one demand change, and defends it with the figures and its likely saving. The student also maps the program of study for one job, such as a utility line worker (apprenticeship), a water plant operator (certificate and a state license), a power plant operator (long on-the-job training) and a utility engineer (four-year study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-energy-resources-clean-energy | Field task day. The student sizes a solar array for an invented school from a dated monthly use table and a given output per panel, finds the years to pay back from given costs, and defends the size with the figures. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a solar installer (apprenticeship or certificate), a wind turbine technician (certificate or two-year study) and an energy engineer (four-year study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-energy-resources-conservation | Field task day. From an invented park's trail map and erosion survey ratings, the student plans which sections a crew repairs first within a set number of crew days, and defends the order with the ratings. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a conservation worker (seasonal, on-the-job training), a forest technician (two-year study) and a conservation scientist (four-year study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-energy-resources-ecology-research | Field task day. The student plans a sample survey of an invented plot (number of squares, a data table), works out a count per square meter from given results, states one limit of the sample, and defends the method. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a field technician (two-year study), a wildlife biologist (four-year study) and a research ecologist (graduate study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-energy-resources-environmental-protection | Field task day. The student compares an invented stream's water test results with a given limit, writes the inspector's finding and the next step, and defends the finding with the readings. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as an environmental technician (two-year study), an environmental inspector (four-year study and training) and an environmental engineer (four-year study and a license): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 
g10-sub-energy-resources-resource-extraction | Field task day. The student plans the reclamation of an invented closed gravel pit (topsoil volume, seeding area, cost and schedule) and reads the field's dated job, pay and safety figures, defending the plan with the figures. The student maps the program of study for one job, such as a mining machine operator (on-the-job training), a reclamation technician (two-year study) and a mining or petroleum engineer (four-year study): the high school courses, the training route and the first credential. 

