5:## The course in brief
10:  **Shorter path.** A school at two sessions a week runs 64 sessions (48 hours, APPROACH.md): 60 in units (9, 9, 9, 7, 7, 11 and 8) and the same 4 course-level days. The 32 folds: each cluster's second explore day folds into its first (the three job cards are split across table groups and shared, 14 sessions); the two two-day field tasks (unit 2's stand, unit 3's production line) run in one session each, their planning half moved to the cluster's explore day (2); and the units' own learner-goal days fold into explore, packet, skill or field task days (16). Every cluster keeps one explore session and its field task session, and every unit keeps its plan day (the feedback and revision day), its assessment day and its respond day; no fold takes a feedback or revision day (lesson 21). The short path is the floor: counting the sessions that never fold (21 closing days, 16 field task sessions, 14 explore sessions, unit 7's two packet and two skill days) leaves exactly 5 for unit 1's own teaching, so it has no slack and its unit-by-unit folds are named in the table after these bullets ("Shorter path, unit by unit"). The scope and sequence sets each folded session by day; if its read finds a session overloaded, the fix is a change of breadth or dose, which is Cory's call ("For the lead").
